<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gongsun Du</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 204</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gongsun Du was appointed governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> in 189 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> disintegrated, and made himself its independent ruler from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoyang">Xiangping</a>. He campaigned against Goguryeo and the Wuhuan and extended his control over the Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commandery">commanderies</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, founding the regime that his descendants ruled until 238.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gongsun-du.jpg" alt="Gongsun Du" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:End_of_Han_Dynasty_Warlords.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
